findings.evidence:
Verified with the binary. On a fresh fixture copy, `git -C kit tag main`; `git symbolic-ref --short HEAD` now prints 'heads/main'. Scanning then gave:
- the evidence_dropped warning: '5 evidence items in kit didn't match commit d77bb65';
- kit:repo:kit is gone, and 11 kit:file:* blocks sit at the top level;
- `map --level component` has no kit blocks.

The cause: Ref evidence names `refs/heads/heads/main`, which verify can't find, so the repo node and the 4 directory nodes, whose only evidence is that Ref, are dropped. Because of the snapshot key (correctness-13), deleting the tag doesn't fix that commit's snapshot.
